Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Opt-in diagnostic dumps for siglip-mlir (SHVLA_SIGLIP_H_DUMPS, _REGEMM, _FULL)

what:     frontend/siglip.py emit() and testing/siglip_ref.py layer_reference(). All off unless SHVLA_SIGLIP_H_DUMPS=<n>
          (the emitted module is identical to the unpatched one for layers 1, 2 and the fused variant when it is unset or 0).
          With H_DUMPS=<n> (layer 0 only), n samples of each, all inline with a `softhier.group_barrier` after every dump
          (cluster 0 prints while the others would already run the next op in place):
            OIN = %o after the attention group barrier (what the o-proj gemm reads), WOI / BOI = wo0 / bo0 just before use,
            AOR = %ao after the o-proj gemm (raw), AOB = %ao after add_bias, HCH = %h after the residual add,
          all with seed 203 (= H's), so the same (row, col) points; at the end OEND (= %o again, seed 203), per head OH<h>
          (o column slice) and PH<h> (softmax rows of head h), min(n, 128) samples each; the end-of-program dumps
          X..OUT use max(64, 16 n) samples.
          SHVLA_SIGLIP_H_REGEMM=1 as well: the o-proj gemm runs a second time into %ao (OIN2 = %o, AOR2 = %ao after it).
          SHVLA_SIGLIP_H_FULL=<m> as well: m samples (large m ~ the whole tensor) of q / k / v / o at the end (QF KF VF OF)
          and of q / k / v after their gemm (QG KG VG, raw) and after add_bias (QB KB VB), same points for G / B / F.
          siglip_ref.layer_reference() returns the matching reference keys ONLY when SHVLA_SIGLIP_H_DUMPS is set (`run.py siglip` flags a missing key as MISSING) (OIN OEND OIN2 WOI BOI AOR AOR2 AOB HCH OH<h> PH<h>
          QF KF VF OF QG KG VG QB KB VB); `run.py siglip-mlir` compares every reference key whose tag the device
          printed (and skips the others), so no checker change there.
why:      siglip-mlir rung c fails at H (59/64 samples) and the end-of-program dumps (64 samples, 0.03 % of a tensor) cannot
          say which of gemm / add_bias / add, or which earlier tensor, is the first bad one (add_bias is in place, so %ao is
          only visible mid-program). Dumps and barriers cost ROI time and printf: diagnosis only.
evidence: LOG G3.2-diag7.
upstream: yes (default output unchanged when the variables are unset).
applies-to: softhier-mlir b11cd5fa4f3e717374d1e9ba14442ff302d1f970

---
